{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CFkFp66MTyuXjwDqCKc2ov","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd078-sum\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/sum: Checksum and Count Blocks in a File\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships a BSD sum that differs from GNU sum in default algorithm and output format.\n6\t  GNU sum supports two algorithms: BSD (default, -r) and System V (-s). The Go\n7\t  implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gsum, installed by\n8\t  coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by differential testing\n9\t  via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Compute a checksum and block count for files or stdin.\n13\t  - G2: Support BSD (-r, default) and System V (-s) checksum algorithms.\n14\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gsum via differential testing.\n15\t\n16\trequirements:\n17\t  R1:\n18\t    title: Default checksum computation\n19\t    items:\n20\t      - R1.1:\n21\t          text: Must compute the BSD checksum (16-bit rotating checksum) of each named file by default and print \"CHECKSUM BLOCKS FILENAME\". Block size is 1024 bytes.\n22\t      - R1.2:\n23\t          text: Must read from stdin when no file arguments are given. Stdin output omits the filename.\n24\t      - R1.3:\n25\t          text: Must process multiple files in argument order, printing one line per file.\n26\t      - R1.4:\n27\t          text: Must exit 1 when any named file cannot be opened, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n28\t\n29\t  R2:\n30\t    title: Algorithm selection\n31\t    items:\n32\t      - R2.1:\n33\t          text: -r selects the BSD checksum algorithm (default). The checksum is a 16-bit rotating checksum, block size 1024 bytes.\n34\t      - R2.2:\n35\t          text: -s selects the System V checksum algorithm. The checksum is a 16-bit sum of all bytes, block size 512 bytes. Output format is \"CHECKSUM BLOCKS FILENAME\".\n36\t\n37\t  R3:\n38\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n39\t    items:\n40\t      - R3.1:\n41\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully.\n42\t      - R3.2:\n43\t          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened.\n44\t      - R3.3:\n45\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n46\t\n47\tnon_goals:\n48\t  - cmd/sum does not implement any modern hash algorithms; use sha256sum or cksum --algorithm for that.\n49\t\n50\tacceptance_criteria:\n51\t  - id: AC1\n52\t    criterion: \"sum on a known file produces the correct BSD checksum and block count, matching gsum.\"\n53\t    traces:\n54\t      - R1.1\n55\t      - R1.2\n56\t      - R1.3\n57\t      - R1.4\n58\t  - id: AC2\n59\t    criterion: \"sum -s on a file produces the System V checksum and block count, matching gsum -s.\"\n60\t    traces:\n61\t      - R2.1\n62\t      - R2.2\n63\t  - id: AC3\n64\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gsum passes for all required test cases.\"\n65\t    traces:\n66\t      - R1.1\n67\t      - R1.2\n68\t      - R1.3\n69\t      - R1.4\n70\t      - R2.1\n71\t      - R2.2\n72\t  - id: AC4\n73\t    criterion: \"cmd/sum compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n74\t    traces:\n75\t      - R1.1\n76\t      - R1.2\n77\t      - R1.3\n78\t      - R1.4\n79\t      - R2.1\n80\t      - R2.2\n81\t      - R3.1\n82\t      - R3.2\n83\t      - R3.3\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"862ebf0f-fea6-4556-8f7a-9640c18df2b5","uuid":"b483547e-7653-4421-ae30-ac2d02287524","timestamp":"2026-05-23T02:39:38.785Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5508/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd078-sum.yaml","content":"id: srd078-sum\ntitle: \"cmd/sum: Checksum and Count Blocks in a File\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships a BSD sum that differs from GNU sum in default algorithm and output format.\n  GNU sum supports two algorithms: BSD (default, -r) and System V (-s). The Go\n  implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gsum, installed by\n  coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by differential testing\n  via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Compute a checksum and block count for files or stdin.\n  - G2: Support BSD (-r, default) and System V (-s) checksum algorithms.\n  - G3: Verify functional parity against gsum via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default checksum computation\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must compute the BSD checksum (16-bit rotating checksum) of each named file by default and print \"CHECKSUM BLOCKS FILENAME\". Block size is 1024 bytes.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: Must read from stdin when no file arguments are given. Stdin output omits the filename.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Must process multiple files in argument order, printing one line per file.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any named file cannot be opened, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Algorithm selection\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: -r selects the BSD checksum algorithm (default). The checksum is a 16-bit rotating checksum, block size 1024 bytes.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: -s selects the System V checksum algorithm. The checksum is a 16-bit sum of all bytes, block size 512 bytes. Output format is \"CHECKSUM BLOCKS FILENAME\".\n\n  R3:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened.\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/sum does not implement any modern hash algorithms; use sha256sum or cksum --algorithm for that.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"sum on a known file produces the correct BSD checksum and block count, matching gsum.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"sum -s on a file produces the System V checksum and block count, matching gsum -s.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gsum passes for all required test cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/sum compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n","numLines":84,"startLine":1,"totalLines":84}}}
