{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user provided a detailed stitch task (Task ID: 5508) from the cobbler orchestrator work queue. The task is to implement srd078 R3.3 for `cmd/sum` - specifically: \"Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\" The task requires modifying `cmd/sum/main.go` and `cmd/sum/sum_test.go`, then verifying compilation and tests pass. The acceptance criteria are: AC1 (R3.3 implemented), AC2 (compiles), AC3 (go vet clean), AC4 (tests pass).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU `sum` utility (BSD and System V checksums)\n   - Differential testing against Homebrew `gsum` reference binary via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` to match GNU coreutils behavior (exit 0 on broken pipe)\n   - The cobbler-scaffold pipeline: measure (task planning) → stitch (code generation)\n   - Git is managed externally by the orchestrator - no git commands allowed\n   - Copyright header required: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max\n   - File size limit: 500 lines max\n   - Write all files before building/testing\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd078-sum.yaml`\n     - The SRD defining R3.3: \"Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\"\n     - R3 group contains R3.1 (exit 0 on success), R3.2 (exit 1 on file open failure), R3.3 (SIGPIPE)\n     - Non-goals: no modern hash algorithms\n   \n   - `cmd/sum/main.go` (existing, 113 lines)\n     - **CRITICAL FINDING**: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` is ALREADY called on line 16 as the first statement in `main()`\n     - Already imports `\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"`\n     - Contains `compute()`, `printLine()`, `bsdChecksum()`, `sysVChecksum()` functions\n     - Full existing main function:\n       ```go\n       func main() {\n           sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n           flag.Bool(\"r\", false, \"\")\n           sysV := flag.Bool(\"s\", false, \"\")\n           flag.Parse()\n           files := flag.Args()\n           exitCode := 0\n           // ... stdin/file processing logic\n           os.Exit(exitCode)\n       }\n       ```\n\n   - `cmd/sum/sum_test.go` (existing, 182 lines)\n     - **CRITICAL FINDING**: `TestSIGPIPE` already exists (lines 152-181) testing SIGPIPE handling\n     - `TestDiff` has comprehensive differential tests for R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.2\n     - TestSIGPIPE creates a large file, starts sum, reads 1 byte, closes stdout pipe, verifies exit 0\n     - Full TestSIGPIPE:\n       ```go\n       func TestSIGPIPE(t *testing.T) {\n           goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n           dir := t.TempDir()\n           largePath := filepath.Join(dir, \"large.dat\")\n           if err := os.WriteFile(largePath, bytes.Repeat([]byte(\"x\\n\"), 500000), 0o644); err != nil {\n               t.Fatal(err)\n           }\n           ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 5*time.Second)\n           defer cancel()\n           cmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, goBin, largePath)\n           stdout, err := cmd.StdoutPipe()\n           if err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n           if err := cmd.Start(); err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n           buf := make([]byte, 1)\n           if _, err := io.ReadFull(stdout, buf); err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n           stdout.Close()\n           err = cmd.Wait()\n           if ctx.Err() == context.DeadlineExceeded {\n               t.Fatal(\"sum timed out; SIGPIPE handler may not be installed\")\n           }\n           if err != nil {\n               t.Fatalf(\"expected exit 0 on SIGPIPE, go